_Unification/working/Doc A - Account & Renewal Memo.md:27:KBM's 5-year prepayment is a financial asset that does not transfer if the account is abandoned. Walking away from it to consolidate inside Pivot's account would mean writing off the prepaid value and continuing to pay annual fees indefinitely — the worst possible combination. Continuing inside KBM and letting Pivot's contract lapse at renewal preserves the asset and removes a recurring cost.
