Financial Management/KBMH/3 Output/BRD_FinancialManagement_v1.0.md:660:KB+Hoag has never implemented finance charges on customer invoices despite having the capability in Core. Finance charges remain available as a "threat" for delinquent customers but are rarely (if ever) applied. Customer deposits are collected and tracked outside the invoice system.
Financial Management/KBMH/3 Output/BRD_FinancialManagement_v1.0.md:666:Pro forma invoices in NetSuite create a non-revenue-recognizing transaction linked to a customer liability account. When a customer makes a deposit, a pro forma invoice is generated with the deposit amount coding to the liability account. The liability is reduced and revenue recognized when the final invoice is generated and the deposit is applied. This standardizes the deposit process, creates an audit trail, and ensures deposit accounting is correct and traceable.
Financial Management/KBMH/3 Output/BRD_FinancialManagement_v1.0.md:672:For deposits: When a customer provides a deposit, a pro forma invoice is generated for the deposit amount, coding to the AR liability account. When the final invoice is generated, the deposit pro forma is automatically applied, reducing the invoice amount and eliminating the deposit liability.
